Lab 20: Final Project: Deploy and Manage Microservices in OpenShift Service Mesh
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Deploy a complete microservice-based application using OpenShift Service Mesh
Implement traffic management policies including canary routing, load balancing, timeouts, and circuit breakers
Configure security policies including mutual TLS and authorization
Diagnose and independently fix a broken traffic routing configuration using Istio diagnostic tools
Test fault resilience mechanisms and explain the observable behavior of circuit breakers
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with OpenShift CLI (oc) commands
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Understanding of microservices architecture principles
Basic networking concepts (HTTP, TCP, load balancing)
Experience with containerized applications
