Task 1: Deploy the Microservice Application with Service Mesh
Subtask 1.1: Verify Service Mesh Installation and Create the Project
First, confirm that OpenShift Service Mesh is installed and running, then create a project and add it to the mesh.

# Check if Service Mesh operators are installed
oc get csv -n openshift-operators | grep -E "(servicemesh|jaeger|kiali)"

# Verify Service Mesh Control Plane
oc get smcp -n istio-system

# Check if all Istio components are running
oc get pods -n istio-system

# Create a new project for the application
oc new-project bookinfo-mesh

# Add the project to the service mesh member roll
cat <<EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: maistra.io/v1
kind: ServiceMeshMemberRoll
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: istio-system
spec:
  members:
  - bookinfo-mesh
EOF

# Enable automatic sidecar injection for the namespace
oc label namespace bookinfo-mesh istio-injection=enabled --overwrite

# Verify the project is added to the mesh
oc get smmr -n istio-system -o yaml
